{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1549995-your-favorite-comic-book-stories","id":1549995,"title":"Your favorite comic book stories?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-04-09T22:08:31-07:00","id":1549995,"title":"Your favorite comic book stories?","content":"Just something fun to lighten up the mood.<br /> <br /> Myself I enjoyed Frank Miller's Batman Year One, Dark Knight Returns and his Sin City series.<br /> <br /> All Star Superman from Grant Morrison.<br /> <br /> Batman The Killing Joke by Alan Moore.<br /> <br /> Batman The Long Halloween by Jeph Loeb<br /> <br /> Judge Dredd Origins by Wagnar.<br /> <br /> Astro City Life In The Big City and Confessions by Kurt Busiek.<br /> <br /> Kingdom Come by Mark Waid and Alex Ross<br /> <br /> All Hail Megatron by Shane McCarthy and Megatron Origin by Eric Holmes.<br /> <br /> Transformers Regeneration One and in general I love Simon Furmon Transformers stuff in general. <br /> Incredible Hulk Future Imperfect by Peter David.<br /> <br /> Green Lantern Rebirth by Geoff Johns.<br /> <br /> What are some of your picks?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 04-10-2025, 10:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-10T18:49:56-07:00","id":1550019,"title":"","content":"A lot of John Ostrander's work for DC, especially his run of Suicide Squad in the 80s and on The Spectre and Martian Manhunter in the 90s. <br /> <br /> Dennis O'Neil's run on The Question.<br /> <br /> Marv Wolfman and George Perez's New Teen Titans.<br /> <br /> Mike Barr and Jim Aparo's Batman &amp; The Outsiders.<br /> <br /> Archie Goodwin's Manhunter.<br /> <br /> James Robinson's Starman.<br /> <br /> Jamie Delano's original run on Hellblazer.<br /> <br /> Alan Moore's Swamp Thing, as well as some of his other stuff (From Hell and Tom Strong, especially).<br /> <br /> Peter Milligan and Chris Bachalo's Shade the Changing Man.<br /> <br /> Grant Morrison's Doom Patrol and The Invisibles.<br /> <br /> Christopher Priest's run on Black Panther.<br /> <br /> Walt Simonson's run on Thor.<br /> <br /> Louise Simonson's work on Power Pack, X-Factor, and New Mutants.<br /> <br /> Chris Clairemont's early X-Men and New Mutants.<br /> <br /> Kurt Busiek's work on Astro City, The Avengers, Thunderbolts, and the Avengers/JLA crossover.<br /> <br /> Fabian Nicieza's initial run on The New Warriors.<br /> <br /> Gene Yang's American Born Chinese, Boxers &amp; Saints, and Superman Smashes the Klan.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-10T19:16:41-07:00","id":1550020,"title":"","content":"James Robinson Starman was awesome and I did enjoy Tom Strong and Top 10 by Alan Moore back in the day.<br /> <br /> In fact James Robinson Starman was one of the few good things that came out of Dan Jurgens Zero Hour mini series.<br /> <br /> I should add that I liked Mark Waid run on the Flash and his Irredeemable series from Boom Studio's.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 04-10-2025, 10:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-12T18:25:14-07:00","id":1550086,"title":"","content":"One thing about Zero Hour was that it was immediately followed by Zero Month, which had Issue 0s for all of DC's titles, which provided excellent jumping on points for new readers. I think that was also when Impulse got spun off in his own series from Mark Waid's Flash run. <br /> <br /> I will give mention to Alan Moore's run on Supreme, which took Rob Liefeld's really terrible Superman knock off and turned it into a vehicle for examining all of the Silver Age stuff DC jettisoned from the character with John Byrne's post-Crisis Man of Steel reboot. Moore also did a Youngblood miniseries called Judgment Day that is both a murder mystery and a millennia spanning story that is meant to give a history to Liefeld's Awesome Comics universe by incorporating a wide swath of historical comic genres.<br /> <br /> And speaking of Byrne, his work on the original Alpha Flight is really good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-12T19:36:36-07:00","id":1550088,"title":"","content":"I do have soft spot for Rob Liefeld even if his artwork is over the top and his writing is mediocre. He comes across as a likeable dude and that one of the reasons he went into the business was because his Dad got ill and he wanted to help out with the bills.<br /> <br /> I can't knock him for that reason.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-12T19:55:46-07:00","id":1550089,"title":"","content":"Back to topic at hand I also liked All Star Western by Justin Gray and Jimmy Palmiotti.<br /> <br /> Jonah Hex Two Gun Mojo by Joe R. Lansdale.<br /> <br /> 100 Bullets by Brian Azzarello.<br /> <br /> Preacher by Garth Ennis. <br /> Ninjak by Matt Kindt.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-14T16:08:47-07:00","id":1550121,"title":"","content":"I always liked <i>Dark Horse Presents</i>, because the stories were different comic-book stories and short.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-22T17:36:25-07:00","id":1550327,"title":"","content":"I have been enjoying stuff from Dynamite Publishing, Boom Studios, Image Comics or Yukito Kishiro Battle Angel Alita.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_lin